wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d6) testing; urgency=medium

  * wiz3d-launch moves a 32-bit game that does not run in its 64-bit
    prefix (on evidence: a 16-bit program by its header, Wine's own
    words about its WoW64 mode in the output, or an end within 30 s with
    a bad status) to a 32-bit prefix beside it, made then, says why, and
    remembers the choice per game in ~/.local/state/wiz3d/prefixes.json
    (WIZ3D_FALLBACK=0 or --no-fallback turns it off). Proven with
    SimCity Classic's 16-bit setup, which wine32 runs and WoW64 does
    not.
  * A game that draws both eyes itself: wiz3d-launch --native-stereo
    LAYOUT (the frame packings of H.264 Table D-8 and Matroska
    StereoMode, and the anaglyphs) keeps wiz3D out, tells the system's
    DXVK the packing (dxvk.stereoInput, dxvk 2.7.1-4+stereo3d3), which
    unpacks it to full side by side, and wiz3d-run --native-stereo
    declares the game's window. Depends on dxvk 2.7.1-4+stereo3d3.
    Tests: test-launch.py (fallback and native cases), test-kwin-
    packed.sh (every packing through the real KWin and DXVK, with the
    control and a negative).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:11:12 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d5) testing; urgency=medium

  * wiz3d-launch makes a missing WINEPREFIX (WINEARCH's architecture, the
    system's DXVK through dxvk-setup, Microsoft's d3dx9 and d3dcompiler_43
    through winetricks when installed, the user folders inside the prefix,
    winemenubuilder off, Z: kept) and runs the game in the folder of its .exe
    (TrackMania Nations Forever quits with status 0 from any other folder).
  * A 32-bit prefix (WINEARCH=win32) gets the x86 tree in its system32.
  * Paths handed to wiz3D follow the prefix's drives or use Wine's
    \\?\unix\ form, so a prefix without Z: works.
  * wiz3d-run and wiz3d-launch run on /usr/bin/python3 (Debian's Python
    policy; a conda environment first on PATH broke them).
  * Depends on dxvk 2.7.1-4+stereo3d2 (dxvk-setup serves 32-bit prefixes);
    recommends the edition's wine (the wrapper picks wine32 for a 32-bit
    prefix) and winetricks.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d4) testing; urgency=medium

  * wiz3d-run uses the shared stereo_declare module (python3-stereo-declare
    1.2.0, from libstereo-declare) instead of carrying its own copy of the
    declaration; what it does and prints is unchanged.
  * New: wiz3d-launch, which puts wiz3D in a Wine prefix beside DXVK, runs
    the game through wiz3d-run and takes wiz3D out again (WIZ3D_LOG_DIR keeps
    wiz3D's logs out of the prefix and the game folder).
  * The fork is now github.com/Sparky-OS/wiz3D (Vcs fields).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d3) testing; urgency=medium

  * The proxy and the wrapper take the real Direct3D 9 from d3d9_real.dll
    when it sits beside the proxy, so a Wine prefix manager can install
    wiz3D in the prefix as it installs DXVK.
  * WIZ3D_LOG_DIR moves wiz3D's log files and Statistic.xml out of the game
    folder and the prefix.
  * Built from the fork rebased on effcol/wiz3D main (Linux build merged
    upstream in #33).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Packaging of the Sparky Stereo OS fork (danielcamposramos/wiz3D, branch
    partner/wiz3d-proton, upstream effcol/wiz3D v0.3.1): Direct3D 9 chain
    built with clang-cl and xwin, full side by side as the only output
    plug-in, wiz3d-run launcher declaring through libstereo-declare.

